ures  in much of the world  people grow up with the idea that  all individuals and all governments are  made up of good and evil impulses and  these come out in different proportions  depending on circumstances  the dallas brothers did not believe this  the world really was divided uh between  the forces of light  and the forces of darkness  so this was one of the key  forces that shaped the dulles brothers  the second was their upbringing  at the very pinnacle of the american  elite  so these boys grew up in the town of  watertown new york up on the shores of  lake ontario it's a kind of a playground  for the new york rich  and their father was the pastor there  every morning during the summer time  they would get up early and take a cold  shower the only kind their father  reverend dulles permitted uh  they would say their prayers with their  father's guidance sing a couple of hymns  and then they were free to rush down to  the shores of the lake  where their two  beloved older relatives were waiting to  take them out on little boats to stalk  the wily smallmouth bass  uh who were those two relatives these  were the two figures that were the  dominant influences in the lives of the  young boys as they grew up  one of them was their grandfather  john watson foster  he was a former secretary of state  he had been secretary of state in the  1890s  and in fact  he was the first secretary of state to  preside over the american overthrow of a  foreign government  uh it was he who was secretary of state  when the united states launched its  operation to overthrow the government of  hawaii and bring hawaii into the united  states  so  the family got into the regime change  business even before the dulles brothers  were born  grandfather foster as they called him  had been a pioneer who had tamed the  wilderness and gone out west an exemplar  of uh  the idea of manifest destiny  think of how  this span of time passed in the space  just from the grandfather to the  grandson